// A carrying frame. One more thing in the arms, for one person.
//
// The plainest kit in the pack and deliberately so: `carry_capacity` is
// 3, and this makes it 4 for whoever is wearing it. A quarter more per
// trip on the same stairs, which is `DESIGN.md` insight 1 answered by
// equipment rather than by architecture — cheaper than a shaft and much
// smaller, and it stacks with nothing.
//
// It is also the kit that competes with a posting: a porter in a harness
// is somebody you have decided is a porter. Standing them in a mill
// wastes it.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
ItemDef(
    id: "item.porters_harness",
    name: "Porter's harness",
    glyph: "🎒",
    order: 41,
    kit: KitDef(
        carry_bonus: 1,
    ),
)
